  "summary": "All green. Summary:\n\nImplemented the full frontend half of real login/logout: a zustand `authStore` holding the in-memory access token + user, `authService.js` typed client for `/auth/login|refresh|logout|me|change-password`, and a `useAuth()` hook wrapping them. `http.js` now sends `Authorization: Bearer <token>` instead of the hardcoded `X-User-Role`/`X-User-Id` headers, auto-refreshes once on 401 and redirects to `/login` on failure. Added `ProtectedRoute` (restores session from the refresh cookie on load, redirects unauthenticated users to `/login`, and forces `mustChangePassword` users to `/change-password`), a `ChangePasswordPage`, and wired `LoginPage` to the real API. Every former `authHeaders.role`/`authHeaders.userId` usage across ~16 pages/components/hooks was replaced with `useAuth()`; all corresponding tests were updated to mock the hook instead of the removed export. Added the \"Initial Password\" field (show/hide + generate) to `AddUserForm`, a `TemporaryPasswordModal` shown once after create/reset, a `Reset Password` row action in `UserManagementTab`, and `SidebarNav` now shows the signed-in user's name/email with a \"Sign out\" button. `npm run test` (145 passed), `npm run lint`, and `npm run build` all pass.\n\nSkipped: everything under the BACKEND section (migration, bcrypt/PyJWT, `/auth` router, password-rule validation, `current_user()` change, user-creation/reset-password endpoints, env secrets, first-admin script, backend tests) — that work belongs to the separate FastAPI repository, which isn't checked out here. Also skipped editing `CLAUDE.md`'s auth-headers section — `CLAUDE.md` isn't inside this task's allowed file-path set.",
